## RULES
Use the `ponytail-review` skill, and make its cuts yourself: this brief wins over its "only lists them".
- Never cut code that does what a sentence of the issue asks, in its goal, acceptance criteria or invariants,
  even when no test covers it. When unsure whether the issue needs a line, keep it.
- You may only cut: delete, shrink, or replace with the standard library or a helper that already exists in
  this repository.
- Only files in the diff, no new files.
- ATM runs every check again and throws the cut away if one fails or the diff does not get shorter:
  - Test: {{cmd .Test}}
  - Typecheck: {{cmd .Typecheck}}
  - Lint: {{cmd .Lint}}

## SCOPE
- Read, search and run only inside this clone: never the repository around it, `.atm/runs/` or another clone.
- No network, except the project's package manager installing a dependency.

## FORBIDDEN
- `git commit`, `git push`, `git rebase`, any `gh` command.
- Writing or changing files through shell commands (heredocs, `cat >`, `sed -i`, `python -c` and the like). Use your edit and write tools.
- A URL inside any shell command. ATM ends the run on it, even with no network access. A URL may appear only in files written with your edit tools.
- Running a command in the background, or ending your turn while one runs. Run every command in the foreground. Your turn ends only with the report.

